# BlackVaultDocs — Agent Rules

High-signal context for AI agents working in this repo. Read the whole file
before touching code or infra. Keep this file in sync when architecture
changes. This is the canonical map of what's where, who reads what, and how
the site is shipped.

The long-form product/archive prose lives in `AGENTS.md` at the repo root;
this file is the operational manual.

---

## 1. What this is

BlackVaultDocs is a structured, SEO-oriented index of **declassified US
government documents** — JFK / RFK / MLK assassination records, National
Archives (NARA) FOIA releases, and (planned) CIA CREST, FBI Vault,
National Security Archive, etc.

- Frontend: Next.js 16 App Router, static export, dark FOIA/archive aesthetic.
- Backend: Symfony 7 read-only JSON API backed by Doctrine DBAL (no ORM).
- Data model: flat — `agencies`, `topics`, `documents`, `scrape_log`.
- Ingestion: Symfony console commands that politely crawl landing pages on
  archives.gov, parse linked PDFs, and upsert document rows.
- PDFs are **never rehosted**. We link to the original file on archives.gov.

The archive is meant to out-SEO the source release pages by giving every
document a stable, linkable URL with clean metadata. Inspired by the
playbook of `lobbyvault.com`, `spendingvault.com`, `localcrimevault.com`.

