## 3. Live infrastructure

### 3.1 Production layout

| Surface | Where it runs | DNS | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Marketing site | S3 bucket `blackvaultdocs.com` behind CloudFront `E2I87T26ZZLVBA` | `blackvaultdocs.com`, `www.blackvaultdocs.com` → CloudFront | Static export from `frontend/out/`, `aws s3 sync out/ s3://blackvaultdocs.com/ --delete` then CloudFront invalidation. |
| Public API | Apache + PHP-FPM on the Sites server (`sshnewbe`) | `api.blackvaultdocs.com` → `52.73.80.160` | vhost: `/etc/apache2/sites-enabled/apache-api.blackvaultdocs.com*.conf`. DocumentRoot: `/var/www/blackvaultdocs.com/backend/public`. Let's Encrypt cert auto-renewed by certbot. |
| Database | Amazon RDS MySQL 8 — `main-instance-1.cf9pnycgvp6w.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com`, DB `blackvaultdocs` | (private) | Shared RDS cluster used by every `seo_sites`-style Range site. |
| Repo on server | `/var/www/blackvaultdocs.com/` owned by `ubuntu:ubuntu` | — | Pulled from `git@github.com:brettev/blackvaultdocs.git` (`main`). |

### 3.2 SSH

The Sites server has a zsh alias defined in the operator's `~/.zshrc`:

```zsh
alias sshnewbe="ssh -i /Users/brettevanson/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox-Personal/Sync\ Stuff/newbrettev.cer ubuntu@52.73.80.160"
```

Always reach the server via `sshnewbe` (or `sshnewbe2` for the secondary IP).
When running one-liners from the agent, use the full `ssh -i "..." ubuntu@52.73.80.160 "..."` form because `sshnewbe` isn't on the agent's PATH.

### 3.3 Database credentials

**Read/write user (Symfony uses this)**

`backend/.env` ships with:

```
DATABASE_URL="mysql://seo_sites:RangeSeoSites2026@main-instance-1.cf9pnycgvp6w.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com:3306/blackvaultdocs?serverVersion=8.0&charset=utf8mb4"
```

`seo_sites` is the shared Range service user (also used by peptidedive,
fatnotmuscle, lobbyvault, etc.). It needs an explicit grant on
`blackvaultdocs.*`:

```sql
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON `blackvaultdocs`.* TO `seo_sites`@`%`;
FLUSH PRIVILEGES;
```

If you ever see a 500 with
`Access denied for user 'seo_sites'@'%' to database 'blackvaultdocs'` from
`api.blackvaultdocs.com`, the grant is missing. Re-apply it as root from
the server:

```bash
sshnewbe
mysql -e 'GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON `blackvaultdocs`.* TO "seo_sites"@"%"; FLUSH PRIVILEGES;'
```

**MySQL root credentials** live in `~ubuntu/.my.cnf` on the Sites server.
Don't copy them off the server and don't echo them in chat or commits.

A secondary dedicated user `blackvaultdocs_user@%` also exists for
isolation — currently unused. Prefer `seo_sites` for consistency with the
rest of the portfolio.

### 3.4 AWS

- **S3 bucket**: `s3://blackvaultdocs.com/` — static site contents. Hosted in `us-east-1`.
- **CloudFront distribution**: `E2I87T26ZZLVBA` — aliases `blackvaultdocs.com` and `www.blackvaultdocs.com`, origin `blackvaultdocs.com.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com`.
- **RDS cluster**: `main.cluster-cf9pnycgvp6w.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com` (writer endpoint), `main-instance-1.cf9pnycgvp6w.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com` (single instance endpoint used in `.env`).
- **ACM / Route 53**: managed via the parent Range AWS account. Certs for `api.blackvaultdocs.com` are Let's Encrypt on the EC2 host; the apex cert is ACM behind CloudFront.
- **Local AWS CLI context** has `s3:ListBucket`, `s3 sync`, and CloudFront read. The on-server IAM role `FNM-EC2-Deploy` (attached to the EC2 instance) can read S3 but **cannot** list or invalidate CloudFront — always run CloudFront invalidations from a developer laptop.

Deploy from a laptop:

```bash
cd frontend
npm ci
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=https://api.blackvaultdocs.com npm run build
aws s3 sync out/ s3://blackvaultdocs.com/ --delete \
  --cache-control "public, max-age=300, s-maxage=3600"
aws cloudfront create-invalidation --distribution-id E2I87T26ZZLVBA --paths '/*'
```

